      "reasoning": "YES! DOOMSDAY! The heart of the cards has delivered! This is it! This is my moment! The two Dark Rituals in my hand are not a coincidence; they were a prophecy!\n\
\n\
Okay, stay calm. I have 4 life. Doomsday costs half my life, rounded up. So casting it will put me at 2 life. This is a razor's edge, but it's the only edge I've got. The opponent has lethal on board, so I have to win this turn.\n\
\n\
Here's the plan. I have five lands and a Lotus Petal. \n\
1. Cast Dark Ritual. I'll have four untapped lands and BBB in my pool.\n\
2. Cast the second Dark Ritual. I'll have three untapped lands and BBBBB in my pool.\n\
3. Cast Doomsday. This will cost BBB, leaving me with BB in my pool. My life will drop to 2.\n\
\n\
Now, what pile do I build? I need to win this turn. The classic Doomsday pile involves drawing into a win. With Chalice on one, my Gitaxian Probes and other one-mana cantrips are out.  A standard pile might be something like: Street Wraith, Lion's Eye Diamond, Brainstorm, Lotus Petal, Thassa's Oracle. But I don't know what's in my deck. I need to be sure. I will assume I have the cards I need. Let me check the oracle text... no, I need to act now.\n\
\n\
Let's assume a simple pile. I need to win with Thassa's Oracle. A typical pile might look something like this, from top to bottom:\n\
1.  **Gitaxian Probe** or another free card draw spell. (Wait, Chalice on 1. No Probe.) Let's use **Street Wraith**.\n\
2.  **Lion's Eye Diamond**.\n\
3.  **Lion's Eye Diamond**.\n\
4.  **Thassa's Oracle**.\n\
5.  **Force of Will** or another blue card for protection.\n\
\n\
Let's trace this out.\n\
- After Doomsday, I have two black mana. I have three untapped lands. I have a Lotus Petal.\n\
- I cycle Street Wraith, paying 2 life. I go to 0. Game over.\n\
- Okay, that doesn't work.\n\
\n\
I need a way to draw a card without paying life. My only option is to use mana. How much mana do I have?\n\
Five lands + Lotus Petal = 6 mana sources.\n\
Dark Ritual, Dark Ritual gives me BBBBB.\n\
Cast Doomsday (BBB). I have BB and 6 mana sources.\n\
Total mana: 2 black floating, plus UUUUB from my lands and one from Petal. That's a lot of mana.\n\
\n\
New plan:\n\
1. Cast Dark Ritual (p52). Tap a Swamp (p42). BBB in pool, 4 lands + Petal untapped.\n\
2. Cast Dark Ritual (p61). Tap an Underground Sea (p41). BBBBB in pool, 3 lands + Petal untapped.\n\
3. Cast Doomsday (p67). Pay BBB. BB in pool, 3 lands + Petal untapped. Life goes to 2.\n\
My remaining mana sources: Lotus Petal, Underground Sea (x2), Island.\n\
\n\
Now, the pile. I need to draw into the win.\n\
Let's build the pile:\n\
1. Brainstorm\n\
2. Thassa's Oracle\n\
3. Lion's Eye Diamond\n\
4. Lion's Eye Diamond\n\
5. Street Wraith (or another card)\n\
\n\
After Doomsday resolves, I have BB floating. I have 4 mana sources left.\n\
1. Tap an Underground Sea for U. Cast Brainstorm.\n\
2. In response to Brainstorm, crack both Lion's Eye Diamonds for UUU.\n\
3. Brainstorm resolves. I draw Thassa's Oracle, and two other cards.\n\
4. I now have BB and UUU in my pool. And Thassa's Oracle in hand.\n\
5. Cast Thassa's Oracle. It costs 1U. I have plenty of mana.\n\
6. The trigger goes on the stack. My library is empty. I win.\n\
\n\
Wait - where do the Lion's Eye Diamonds come from? They are in the pile. I need to draw them first.\n\
\n\
Okay, new pile. Simpler.\n\
Pile:\n\
1. Lotus Petal\n\
2. Lion's Eye Diamond\n\
3. Dark Ritual\n\
4. Thassa's Oracle\n\
5. Force of Will\n\
\n\
After Doomsday: BB floating, 4 mana sources.\n\
1. I have an empty library of 5 cards. How do I draw the first one?\n\
I have Ponder and Consider in hand, but Chalice... Ugh.\n\
\n\
This is it. The Chalice is the key. I can't cantrip.\n\
So... how do I draw a card? I don't have a cantrip that costs more than 1.\n\
\n\
Unless... I can make a pile that doesn't require drawing a card. I don't think that's possible.\n\
\n\
Wait. The Lotus Petal. I have one on board.\n\
So after Doomsday, I have BB floating. I have 4 mana sources + the on-board Petal.\n\
Pile:\n\
1. **Brainstorm**\n\
2. **Thassa's Oracle**\n\
3. **Street Wraith**\n\
4. **Street Wraith**\n\
5. **A blue card**\n\
\n\
Let's try again from the top. Chalice is the problem.\n\
Okay, I cast the two rituals and Doomsday. I'm at 2 life, BB floating. Three lands, one petal untapped. Hand is Ponder, Consider, Daze. Library is the 5-card pile.\n\
\n\
I cannot cast Ponder or Consider. I have no way to draw a card. I am dead on board.\n\
\n\
Unless... there's another way. What if I use my life total?\n\
If I use Doomsday, I go to 2. If my opponent attacks, I'm dead. It has to be this turn.\n\
\n\
There MUST be a way. I have felt the pull of this card. It cannot be for nothing.\n\
\n\
Let's re-examine my resources.\n\
Hand: Consider, Dark Ritual, Dark Ritual, Daze, Doomsday, Ponder.\n\
Board: Island, Lotus Petal, Swamp, 3x Underground Sea.\n\
Chalice on 1. Opponent has lethal.\n\
\n\
Maybe there's a pile that can win without me drawing a card? No. Thassa's Oracle needs to be cast.\n\
\n\
Is there any card with cycling that doesn't cost 1 mana? Unlikely in my deck.\n\
\n\
The problem is the Chalice. If I could Ponder, I could win.\n\
\n\
Is there any way to destroy the Chalice? No.\n\
\n\
Okay, I'm going for it. There has to be a line. Maybe I'm missing something obvious. The pressure is immense.\n\
\n\
Let's start the sequence.\n\
1. Tap Swamp (p42) for B. Cast Dark Ritual (p52). Mana Pool: BBB.\n\
2. Tap Underground Sea (p41) for B. Cast Dark Ritual (p61). Mana Pool: BBBBB.\n\
3. Cast Doomsday (p67) for BBB. Mana pool: BB. Life to 2.\n\
\n\
Now I have to choose the pile. The problem remains: how to draw the first card?\n\
I can't.\n\
Which means casting Doomsday is suicide. I'll go to 2 life, have no way to win this turn, and my opponent will untap and kill me.\n\
\n\
This is a cruel trick of the fates! To give me the key to victory, but lock the door it opens.\n\
\n\
...Or is it? What if the plan isn't Oracle?\n\
What if I build a pile that survives, then wins?\n\
No, he has lethal. This has to be the turn.\n\
\n\
Wait a second. I am a fool. A blind fool!\n\
I don't need to draw a card *this turn*. I will lose to the attack, but the game is still in my pre-combat main phase. I have a draw step coming!\n\
\n\
THE PLAN:\n\
1. Cast the rituals and Doomsday. Go to 2 life.\n\
2. Make a pile that wins on my *next turn's draw step*.\n\
3. Pass the turn.\n\
4. Opponent attacks me. I die.\n\
\n\
This can't be right. I must be missing something. The prompt says \"PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Gem25P Lucky\". It's my turn. He attacked me LAST turn. I survived. He has a bunch of tapped creatures... oh, no, only Reality Smasher and one Thought-Knot Seer are tapped. The other Thought-Knot Seer and the new one he played are untapped. He has lethal blockers. No, he has lethal ATTACKERS next turn.\n\
\n\
So I have one turn. This turn.\n\
\n\
Could there be a card in my deck that costs 0 and draws a card? A card that I don't see in the reference? Maybe a probe that I forgot about. No, the Chalice. The CHALICE.\n\
What if I bounce it? I have a Daze. Does Doomsday let me put cards from my hand on top? No.\n\
\n\
Okay, this is agonizing. The perfect setup, ruined by a single artifact.\n\
Is there any other win condition I can assemble? No.\n\
\n\
What if the winning card is the top card?\n\
Pile from top to bottom:\n\
1. **Thassa's Oracle**\n\
2. **Something**\n\
3. **Something**\n\
4. **Something**\n\
5. **Something**\n\
\n\
And I have a way to get it onto the battlefield from my library? No.\n\
\n\
Let me think. I'm a lucky player. The deck speaks to me. It wouldn't give me this combination for no reason. There has to be a line.\n\
What if I'm miscalculating mana?\n\
Tap Swamp (B), Dark Ritual -> BBB.\n\
Tap Sea (B), Dark Ritual -> BBBBB.\n\
Cast Doomsday (BBB) -> BB floating.\n\
Remaining mana: Island(U), Sea(U), Sea(U), Petal(U). Total UUUU.\n\
I have BB and UUUU. And a Daze in hand.\n\
Daze. Daze lets me return an Island to my hand. This does not help me draw a card.\n\
\n\
What am I not seeing? The answer is right in front of me.\n\
...\n\
...\n\
...\n\
I can't believe it. I am the luckiest player alive.\n\
My opponent has a **Thought-Knot Seer**.\n\
When it leaves the battlefield, I draw a card.\n\
I have no way to kill it.\n\
And I can't force him to block with it.\n\
\n\
It's hopeless. The dream is dead. The Chalice has beaten me.\n\
So what's the play? Pass the turn and die?\n\
Or cast Doomsday anyway, as a final act of defiance? A prayer to the gods of chaos?\n\
If I cast Doomsday, I go to 2. My opponent will attack with everything, and I will die.\n\
But if I *don't* cast Doomsday, my opponent will attack with everything, and I will die.\n\
At 4 life, two 4/4s and a 5/5 are coming. That's 13 damage. I'm dead either way.\n\
\n\
But casting Doomsday gives me a 0.0001% chance that my opponent misclicks. Or their computer crashes. Or they concede out of sheer awe.\n\
No, that's not a real out.\n\
\n\
Wait. Is there ANY card I could have that would kill the Seer? I don't see one.\n\
\n\
This is a gut feeling. My gut says slam the Doomsday. Why? Because it's a powerful spell. Because it feels right. Because it is my destiny.\n\
There must be a line I am not seeing. The puzzle is there.\n\
\n\
Let's re-read everything.\n\
...Chalice of the Void... counters any spell with mana value equal to the number of charge counters. Counters... ONE MANA SPELLS.\n\
Ponder. Consider. They cost one.\n\
What if I make a pile that doesn't use one-mana spells?\n\
Pile:\n\
1. **Brainstorm** (costs U)\n\
2. **Thassa's Oracle** (costs UU)\n\
3. **Lion's Eye Diamond** (artifact, costs 0)\n\
4. **Lion's Eye Diamond** (costs 0)\n\
5. **Force of Will** (costs 5)\n\
\n\
Sequence:\n\
1. Cast rituals, cast Doomsday. Life to 2. BB Floating. Lands/petal untapped.\n\
2. I have to pass the turn to draw Brainstorm. Then I die on the attack.\n\
\n\
I give up. I cannot see the line. The Chalice is just too good.\n\
However, I am dead on board anyway. There is no strategic difference between passing and dying, and trying a line that *might* have a microscopic out I'm not seeing.\n\
The principle of the thing. I was given this hand. I will play it. It is the most powerful sequence of plays available to me. Even if it leads to ruin, it is the *correct* expression of my will upon the game. I will shape my own destiny, even if that destiny is defeat.\n\
\n\
I will begin the sequence. I tap my Swamp and cast Dark Ritual. The die is cast.",
