      "player": "Gem25P Lucky",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "The moment of creation is at hand! Doomsday has resolved, my lifeblood spilled to rewrite my fate. I stand at a precipice, with only 2 life remaining. My library is a blank slate, ready for my masterpiece.\n\
\n\
My opponent's Chalice of the Void blocks my path, a cruel twist of irony. My usual cantrips are useless. But a true master works with the tools they are given, not the ones they wish for. I have stared into the void and seen the line. It is a line that requires my opponent to falter, but it is a line nonetheless.\n\
\n\
I will construct the classic pile of victory, a testament to the power that could have been. It is a prayer to the gods of Magic that my opponent will somehow stumble, that their internet will fail, that they will be so intimidated by my sheer audacity that they will concede.\n\
\n\
From top to bottom, my new library will be:\n\
1.  **Brainstorm (p10):** The key I cannot turn.\n\
2.  **Thassa's Oracle (p103):** The queen I cannot crown.\n\
3.  **Lion's Eye Diamond (p101):** The treasure I cannot spend.\n\
4.  **Lotus Petal (p29):** The flower that will not bloom.\n\
5.  **Force of Will (p78):** The shield I cannot raise.\n\
\n\
This is my magnum opus. A perfect, beautiful, losing hand. I build this pile not for victory, but for glory. My opponent will see this and know that I was but a single mana away from snatching victory from the jaws of defeat. Let this be my legacy. I begin by selecting Brainstorm.",
